{"format":"kards-original-reference","version":1,"id":"b50038eebdd87efd","name":"card_event_redeployment","package":"/Game/Blueprints/Cards/Japan/Legions/events/card_event_redeployment","parent":"UBaseCardObject","card":{"title":"REDEPLOYMENT","text":"Shuffle all cards in your hand into your deck, then draw that many cards plus one.","flavorText":"In 1945 the Japanese planned Operation Ketsu-Go, which was an attempt to make a last stand defending the home islands and fight to the bitter end. The Japanese High Command planned to transfer many troops and munitions from the Asian continent and to the home islands, but this proved very difficult due to constant American assaults and followed by a drastic decrease in manpower. Getting the munition ready also proved to be a serious problem due to shortages of resources and technology. For this last stand the Japanese had reserved around 5000 conventional aircraft, 5,500 kamikaze aircraft, 1,300 suicide submarines, hundreds of piloted bombs, manned torpedoes, and variaty of suicide vehicles. In manpower they had raised 56 divisions and 38 brigades, involving around 2,000,000 men. However, the imminent American invasion never took place. Following the detonation of atomic bombs over the cities of Hiroshima and Nagasaki, the Japanese surrendered to the Allies on August 15, 1945.","faction":"Japan","type":"order","rarity":"Uncommon","cost":4,"operationCost":0,"attack":0,"defense":0},"defaults":{"UberGraphFrame":{},"Name":"card_event_redeployment","title":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_redeployment_title","SourceString":"REDEPLOYMENT","LocalizedString":"REDEPLOYMENT"},"Type":"ETypeEnum::order","faction":"EFactionEnum::Japan","kredits":4,"Text":{"Namespace":"card_japan","Key":"card_event_redeployment_text","SourceString":"Shuffle all cards in your hand into your deck, then draw that many cards plus one.","LocalizedString":"Shuffle all cards in your hand into your deck, then draw that many cards plus one."},"flavorT